<title>USA: TENNIS-RESULTS AT MEN'S CLAY COURT CHAMPIONSHIPS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-RESULTS AT MEN'S CLAY COURT CHAMPIONSHIPS.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the $289,250 U.S. Men's Clay Court Championships on Tuesday (prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>1-Michael Chang (U.S.) beat Jan-Michael Gambill (U.S.) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>4-Alex O'Brien (U.S.) beat Gilbert Schaller (Austria) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>6-Chris Woodruff (U.S.) beat Javier Frana (Argentina) 4-6 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>7-Byron Black (Zimbabwe) beat Johan Van Herck (Belgium) 6-3 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>Fernando Meligeni (Brazil) beat Mark Merklein (U.S.) 7-6 (7-3) 7-6 (8-6)</p>
<p>Magnus Norman (Sweden) beat Guillaume Raoux (France) 7-5 2-1 retired. (Raoux suffered a calf injury.)</p>
<p>Marcelo Filippini (Uruguay) beat Wayne Black (Zimbabwe) 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>Grant Stafford (South Africa) beat Thierry Champion (France) 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Juan Albert Viloca (Spain) beat Luke Jensen (U.S. 6-2 6-2</p>
</text>
